---
interface Props {
  topic: "j1-closed" | "passive-renewal" | "family-renewal";
}

const { topic } = Astro.props;

const index = "https://www.livinginandorra.com/index.html";
const catD =
  "https://www.livinginandorra.com/residency_category_d.html#active_update";
const renewals = "https://www.livinginandorra.com/residency_renewals.html";
---

{
  topic === "j1-closed" && (
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        <a href={index} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Living in Andorra
        </a>{" "}
        states, as of its 15 September 2026 index, that Compte Propi /
        official J.1 remains closed to new applications. A
        <a href={catD} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Category D note
        </a>{" "}
        on that site reports a Compte Propi quota closed in October 2025,
        a February 2026 quota of 150 places reported as fully taken on
        the day it opened, and, as of September 2026, no new quota and
        no official news of a change to price or procedure. The same
        note speculates that a reopen may wait until parliamentary
        elections due by March 2027, and that procedure and cost may
        change when that is addressed. That timeline is a practitioner
        report, not a Government notice. Confirm on Govern.ad and the
        quota decree before you treat a place as available.
      </p>
    </div>
  )
}

{
  topic === "passive-renewal" && (
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        Official-verify: the live D.2 list still names, among other
        proofs, a pension certificate, a tax return from the last country
        of residence, and bank certifications.{" "}
        <a href={renewals} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Living in Andorra
        </a>{" "}
        states that Immigration now requires the annual income test to
        be shown by a certificate from an Andorran bank, and that a
        foreign bank certificate or foreign income proof is no longer
        accepted as a substitute. Confirm that practice with counsel
        against the live D.2 text. This site does not treat her income
        multiples as law.
      </p>
    </div>
  )
}

{
  topic === "family-renewal" && (
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        Official-verify: the published B.2 list does not currently name
        a bank solvency certificate.{" "}
        <a href={renewals} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Living in Andorra
        </a>{" "}
        states that, for active residents with dependants (family
        grouping), an Andorran bank certificate of solvency is now
        required at the first renewal as well as at the initial file, and
        that the certificate must be issued on the principal holder’s
        personal account — not a company account and not a joint
        account. Confirm on the live B.2 page and with counsel. We do
        not convert household means tests into salary multiples here.
      </p>
    </div>
  )
}
